ervices", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='full-pen-fabrication-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fun City Foods, Inc. operates from Las Vegas, Nevada The company''s founding year is not publicly stated.

The firm functions as a master food‑service distributor for major brands including Mars, Hershey and Nestlé, and supplements that line with equipment sales and service. It also markets an exclusive private‑label item, Player''s Choice Card Cookies — a shortbread cookie packaged as a full deck of cards — which it describes as being rushed back into production by popular demand. No facility square footage, headcount or annual volume figures are provided.

Customers span the food‑service spectrum, from large accounts carrying national confectionery lines to smaller operators seeking popcorn, candy, snacks and beverages. The company emphasizes "nationwide supply, local availability" and states it serves "big or small" clients alike. Concrete brand examples are the three named suppliers: Mars, Hershey and Nestlé.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food service distribution", "Equipment sales & service", "Private-label product development"], "industries": ["Food service", "Hospitality", "Retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Master distributor for Mars, Hershey & Nestl\u00e9", "Nationwide supply with local availability", "\"We never say no\" service philosophy", "Exclusive Player''s Choice Card Cookies", "Equipment sales and service"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Las Vegas, NV -> db", "President: Lon Ross -> /about", "Master distributor for Mars, Hershey, Nestl\u00e9 -> db", "Equipment sales & service capability -> db", "Exclusive Player''s Choice Card Cookies -> /", "Nationwide supply, local availability -> /", "Serves big and small customers -> /", "\"We never say no\" business model quote -> /about", "Address: 3555 West Reno Ave, Suite C, Las Vegas, NV 89118 -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "Master Food service distributors for Mars, Hershey & Nestle", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fun-city-foods-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Furniture Joint operates from Salt Lake City, Utah, where founder Chad builds custom furniture by hand. A self-described family man with roots in self-reliance, he started the business to create unique, heirloom-quality pieces rather than pursue high-volume sales.

The shop produces handcrafted wooden furniture using traditional joinery methods that maintain the natural integrity of each piece. Chad works primarily with locally sourced wood when possible, focusing on mid-century modern designs while accepting commissions in other styles. Each project begins with a client consultation and progresses through detailed design, with shop visits encouraged throughout the build.

The business serves residential customers seeking custom furnishings such as dining tables, rocking chairs, and porch swings—pieces intended to become part of family life rather than disposable decor. Clients engage directly with the maker from concept through completion.

Chad founded The Furniture Joint to counter the trend of cheap, mass-produced furniture that lasts only a single generation. He emphasizes that furniture should be cherished, not replaced, and that appreciation comes from understanding how a piece is made.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Traditional joinery", "Wood furniture construction", "Client consultation", "Shop visits during production"], "industries": ["Custom furniture", "Residential furniture"], "materials": ["Wood", "Local wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Traditional joinery preserving wood''s natural integrity", "Locally sourced materials when possible", "Client consultation with ongoing shop access during build", "Mid-century modern focus with openness to custom styles", "Heirloom-quality pieces designed to last generations"], "facts_used": ["Salt Lake City, Utah headquarters -> db", "Founder Chad -> /about", "Handcrafted wooden furniture using traditional joinery -> /about", "Focus on mid-century modern custom designs -> /about", "Uses local materials when possible -> /about", "Client consultation with shop visits encouraged -> /about", "Business emphasizes heirloom quality over volume -> /about", "Solo operation implied by first-person narrative -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "hand crafted wooden furniture represents the peculiarity of people and their homes", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='furniture-joint' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='G&G Industries was established in 1992 in Shelby Township, Michigan, initially operating as a fabric die cutter and converter.

The company specializes in honeycomb composite spray molding (CSM) for automotive interior trim and NVH components, operating four CSM cells with ten dedicated presses, two converting presses, and two honeycomb expanders in a 70,000-square-foot facility. It produces over 1.3 million composite panels annually and handles programs ranging from 10,000 to 500,000 units.

The company distinguishes itself as the first North American manufacturer to introduce honeycomb composite spray molding to the automotive sector (2004) and the first to produce load floors using polyurethane CSM technology. Its mission emphasizes becoming the preferred supplier of high-visibility interior trim and NVH components through quality-driven processes and customer satisfaction, guided by values of honesty, simplicity, participation, and continuous improvement.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO/TS 16949:2009','QS9000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Honeycomb Composite Spray Molding", "Insert Molding", "Mechanical Engineering", "Program Management", "Manufacturing Engineering", "Design Capabilities", "Lean Manufacturing Techniques", "Material Resource Planning", "Production Planning", "Product & Process Design", "Waterjet Cutting", "Stamping/Blanking", "Pinch Trim in Mold", "Automated Lamination of Textiles to Substrates", "Manual Lamination of Textiles to Substrates", "Lamination of Decorative Fabrics and Non-wovens", "Thermal Film Lamination", "Roll Coat Adhesive Lamination", "Spray Adhesive Lamination", "Edge-wrapping", "Die Cutting", "Honeycomb Expansion", "Automotive Interior Color Matching and Evaluation", "In-house Calibrated Premium Light Booth"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": ["Polyurethane", "Honeycomb core (paper and other)", "Textiles", "Decorative fabrics", "Non-wovens", "Films", "Foils", "Carpet", "Reinforcements"], "equipment": ["Honeycomb Composite Spray Molding cells (4)", "Dedicated presses (10)", "Converting presses (2)", "Honeycomb expanders (2)", "Waterjet cutting system", "Stamping/blanking equipment", "Pinch trim in-mold tooling", "Calibrated premium light booth (Macbeth Lab)"], "volume": "10,000 to 500,000 units per program; over 1.3 million composite panels annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First North American manufacturer to introduce honeycomb composite spray molding to automotive (2004)", "First North American manufacturer of load floors using polyurethane CSM technology", "Over 1.3 million composite panels produced annually", "IATF 16949:2016 certified quality system", "Handles production programs from 10,000 to 500,000 units"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> /about", "Headquarters Shelby Township, MI -> /", "Initial business: fabric die cutter/converter -> /about", "First mass production sunshade assembly 1996 -> /about", "Macbeth Lab introduced 1999 -> /about", "QS9000 certification 2002 -> /about", "Polyurethane injection molding started 2003 -> /about", "First in NA to introduce honeycomb CSM to automotive 2004 -> /about", "Stabilicore process introduced 2006 -> /about", "First in NA to manufacture load floors using polyurethane CSM 2007 -> /about", "ISO/TS 16949:2009 certification 2010 -> /about", "Exceeded 1,000,000 CSM units annually 2011 -> /about", "In-house paper honeycomb expansion 2015 -> /about", "IATF 16949:2016 certification 2018 -> /about", "Compression molded NVH components production 2022 -> /about", "Facility size 70,000 sq ft -> /about", "Annual production over 1.3 million composite panels -> /about", "CSM cells: 4, dedicated presses: 10 -> /capabilities", "Converting presses: 2 -> /capabilities", "Honeycomb expanders: 2 -> /capabilities", "Waterjet cutting, stamping/blanking, pinch trim in mold -> /capabilities", "Lamination capabilities (automated/manual, thermal film, roll coat, spray adhesive, edge-wrapping) -> /capabilities", "Die cutting -> /capabilities", "Color matching and evaluation since 1999, calibrated light booth -> /capabilities", "Serves OEMs and Tier 1 automotive -> /about", "Vehicle list: Subaru, BMW, Mercedes, GM, Lexus, Toyota, FCA, Ford, Nissan, Honda -> /about", "Mission: preferred supplier of high-visibility interior trim and NVH components -> /", "Values: Honesty, Simplicity, Participation, Continuous Improvement -> /", "Focus fundamentals: Quality, Program Management, Customer Delivery, Customer Value -> /about", "Program volume range 10,000 to 500,000 units -> /about", "Testimonial: zero kanban errors, zero on-time delivery issues (AMI) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "G&G Industries opens for business as a fabric die cutter/converter.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='g-g-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='G5 Textile Group was founded in 1989 in St Cloud, Florida, by Eddie, who serves as CEO and founder. The company began as a global manufacturing operation specializing in apparel and textiles, supplying clothing to major brands worldwide.

The company designs and produces custom-made garments at scale through a network of manufacturing facilities in the United States, El Salvador, China, and Colombia. Its "Smart Manufacture" approach blends advanced technology with customization, supported by an online platform that lets clients customize designs, process orders, and manage custom production. The facilities are equipped for high-volume output while emphasizing eco-friendly materials, energy-efficient technologies, and waste reduction practices.

G5 serves the fashion, athletic wear, and branded merchandise sectors. Its customer base includes professional sports organizations such as the Orlando Magic, for which it produces in-house department uniforms, as well as educational institutions like JPETROV Academy and white-label fashion partners such as TeamIP, which has collaborated for five years on innovative fashion products.

The company states that its differentiation lies in combining innovation, efficiency, and sustainability. It aims to cut production costs and time without sacrificing quality, leveraging global production coordination and a technology-driven customization platform to deliver cost-effective, personalized garment manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom garment design", "Garment manufacturing", "Smart Manufacture (technology-driven customization)", "Global production coordination", "Online customization platform", "Eco-friendly material sourcing", "Energy-efficient production", "Waste reduction practices", "Branded merchandise production", "Athletic wear manufacturing", "White-label fashion production", "Sports team uniform manufacturing"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Textiles", "Fashion", "Athletic wear", "Sports merchandise", "Brand merchandise", "White-label fashion"], "materials": ["eco-friendly materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Smart Manufacture: technology-driven customization platform for garment design and ordering", "Global manufacturing footprint across the United States, El Salvador, China, and Colombia", "Eco-friendly materials, energy-efficient technologies, and waste reduction practices", "Online platform for design customization, order processing, and custom order management", "Focus on cost-effective, efficient production without compromising quality"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 -> db", "Headquarters in St Cloud, Florida -> db", "Global manufacturing company specializing in apparel and textiles -> page \"/\"", "Manufacturing facilities in United States, El Salvador, China, Colombia -> page \"/\" and \"/about-us\"", "Smart Manufacture blending advanced technology with customization -> page \"/about-us\"", "Online platform for customization of designs, processing orders and custom orders -> page \"/\"", "Eco-friendly materials, energy-efficient tech