UPDATE companies SET description='GAMA Electronics was founded in 1990 by John and Irene Golbeck in Woodstock, Illinois, about fifty miles northwest of Chicago. From its inception, the company positioned itself as a full-service electronic products manufacturer serving customers worldwide.

The company designs and manufactures electromechanical and electronic controls, including custom electronic assemblies, switches, control panels, and wireless remote controls. Its Woodstock facility handles both through-hole and surface-mount PCB assembly, mechanical assembly, wire harnessing, and packaging, with production rates ranging from low-volume to high-volume sustained runs. In-house design capabilities span circuit and PCB layout, software development, and mechanical design for sheet metal, injection-molded plastics, graphical overlays, and control panels. Prototyping is performed internally to validate designs before tooling. Global manufacturing alliances supplement U.S. production.

GAMA serves the transportation, industrial equipment, medical, agricultural, and marine markets. In transportation, it produces patented battery disconnect switches and high-volume cruise control switch assemblies for a major U.S. automotive manufacturer. Industrial customers use motor controls, access controls, remote controls, HVAC controls, gymnasium equipment controls, winch and hoist controls, and lighting controls. Medical work includes a line of heat sealers and custom assemblies for X-ray machinery, pharmaceutical dispensing equipment, and patient assist devices. Agricultural applications feature remote control systems, motor control assemblies, and custom control panels.

The company emphasizes a family-oriented workplace culture, stating that happy employees lead to satisfied customers. Its ISO 9001 certification underpins quality assurance, while the combination of a modern U.S. facility and global partnerships aims to deliver competitive pricing and timely delivery. A focus on research and development means the product portfolio reflects both current offerings and engineering capabilities.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Through-hole PCB assembly", "Surface-mount PCB assembly", "Mechanical assembly", "Wire harnessing", "Packaging", "Circuit design", "PCB design", "Software design", "Mechanical design (sheet metal, injection molded plastic, graphical overlay, control panel)", "In-house prototyping", "Custom electronic controls and assemblies", "Wireless remote controls", "Battery disconnect switches", "Cruise control switch assembly", "Medical heat sealer products", "Remote control systems", "Waterproof controls", "Timers", "USB and 120V power management systems", "Industrial control boxes", "Control systems", "Motor controls", "Switches and relays", "Electronic assemblies"], "industries": ["Transportation", "Marine", "Agriculture", "Medical", "Industrial Equipment", "Automotive Accessories"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low volume to high volume sustained production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1990 by John and Irene Golbeck -> /about-us", "Family-owned, managed by founders and son Tom -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Woodstock, Illinois -> /about-us, /capabilities", "Full-service electronic products manufacturer -> /", "ISO 9001 certified -> /about-us", "Capabilities: through-hole and surface-mount PCB assembly, mechanical assembly, wire harnessing, packaging -> /capabilities", "Production rates from low volume to high volume sustained runs -> /capabilities", "Design services: circuit design, PCB design, software design, mechanical design (sheet metal, injection molded plastic, graphical overlay, control panel) -> /capabilities", "In-house prototyping -> /capabilities", "Global manufacturing alliances -> /capabilities", "Industries served: transportation, industrial equipment, medical, agriculture, marine -> /about-us, /", "Transportation products: patented battery disconnect switches, high-volume cruise control switch assemblies for major US automotive manufacturer -> /", "Industrial equipment: motor controls, access controls, remote controls, HVAC controls, gymnasium equipment controls, winch/hoist controls, lighting controls -> /", "Medical: heat sealer products, custom assemblies for X-ray machinery, pharmaceutical dispensing equipment, patient assist devices -> /", "Agriculture: remote control systems, motor control assemblies, custom control panels -> /", "Company culture: family-oriented workplace, happy employees -> /about-us", "Competitive pricing and timely delivery via U.S. facility and global alliances -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a full service electronic products manufacturer.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gama-electronics-plant-2' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='GAO RFID Inc., a member of the GAO Group, is headquartered in Toronto, Canada, with a U.S. office in New York City. The company has over 30 years of experience in RFID and BLE technologies, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The company designs and manufactures a broad range of RFID and BLE hardware, including readers, tags, antennas, printers, and gateways covering low frequency, high frequency, ultra-high frequency, active, and Bluetooth Low Energy spectra. Its software portfolio centers on a proprietary middleware platform that can be customized into industry-specific applications, cloud services, and reporting tools. GAO RFID also provides consulting, site surveys, system integration, and technical support. To date, it has deployed more than 11,000 RFID and BLE systems across over 70 countries.

Customers range from small and mid-sized enterprises to Fortune 500 companies, educational institutions, and government agencies. The company serves industries such as healthcare, agriculture, oil and gas, manufacturing, logistics, transportation, retail, automotive, railway, livestock management, education, data centers, warehousing, and cold-chain monitoring.

GAO RFID emphasizes three differentiators: overnight delivery from local warehouses within the continental U.S. and Canada, expert support with onsite capability, and hardware that is expertly designed, manufactured, and tested in-house. Its team includes CompTIA RFID+ certified professionals who assist from initial consultation through deployment and long-term maintenance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RFID reader manufacturing", "RFID tag manufacturing", "BLE gateway manufacturing", "BLE beacon manufacturing", "RFID antenna manufacturing", "RFID printer integration", "RFID middleware development", "Custom RFID software development", "RFID system integration", "RFID consulting", "RFID site survey", "Technical support", "Warranty service", "Overnight delivery (US/Canada)"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Agriculture", "Oil & Gas", "Manufacturing", "Logistics", "Transportation", "Retail", "Automotive", "Railway", "Livestock Management", "Education", "Government", "Data Centers", "Warehousing", "Supply Chain", "Cold Chain", "Asset Tracking", "Access Control", "People Tracking", "Security Management"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Overnight delivery for stocked items within Continental US & Canada", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Overnight delivery within Continental US & Canada from local warehouse", "Expert support with onsite option", "Quality products expertly designed, manufactured & tested", "Over 11,000 RFID/BLE systems deployed in 70+ countries", "CompTIA RFID+ certified professionals"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Toronto, Canada -> /about", "US office in New York City -> /", "Over 30 years of experience -> /about", "Incorporated in both Canada and the United States -> /about", "Designs and manufactures RFID and BLE hardware -> /", "Offers readers, tags, antennas, printers, gateways across LF, HF, UHF, Active, BLE frequencies -> /", "Proprietary middleware platform for customizable software -> /", "Provides consulting, site surveys, system integration, technical support -> /services", "Deployed over 11,000 RFID/BLE systems in 70+ countries -> /", "Customers include SMEs, Fortune 500, educational and government agencies -> /about", "Serves healthcare, agriculture, oil & gas, manufacturing, logistics, transportation, retail, automotive, railway, livestock, education, data centers, warehousing, supply chain, cold chain, security -> /, /about", "Overnight delivery within Continental US & Canada from local warehouse -> /about", "Expert support with onsite option -> /about", "Quality products expertly designed, manufactured & tested -> /about", "CompTIA RFID+ certified professionals -> /about", "Software customization framework based on 15 years development experience -> /services", "Worldwide experience in hundreds of RFID projects -> /services", "Site survey service for optimal reader/antenna/tag placement -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "GAO RFID Inc. designs and manufactures advanced RFID products", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gao-rfid' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='GEM Equipment of Oregon, Inc. was founded in 1968 in Woodburn, Oregon, by co‑founder Ed McKenney. Starting with limited resources but a clear vision to deliver equipment that meets real‑world processing needs through close collaboration with customers, the company quickly became a key supplier to major food processors. In 2023, GEM was acquired by FPS Food Process Solutions, joining a global family of companies that includes Charlottetown Metal Products and Total Solutions Limited.

The company designs, builds, and installs custom food‑processing equipment, specializing in advanced frying systems. Its product range includes fryers, blanchers, and batter applicators, offered as standalone machines or fully integrated processing lines. Engineering relies on computational fluid dynamics (CFD) modelling to optimize oil flow, and equipment is constructed from stainless steel for durability. GEM also provides a global service network with remote diagnostics, maintenance, and retrofit services.

GEM serves food manufacturers worldwide, with a focus on fried‑food production. Its customer base includes major processors such as General Foods, Ore‑Ida, Simplot, McCain Foods, and Lamb Weston. Applications span potato processing (French fries), seafood, vegetable, snack‑food, and malting operations.

The company’s operating philosophy centers on three principles: lowest total cost of ownership over a ten‑year horizon, exceptional service with urgent field response, and continuous improvement through design and manufacturing enhancements. CFD expertise that eliminates recirculation zones and heat spots is cited as a key differentiator, along with easy access to critical components for efficient sanitation and changeovers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom food processing equipment design", "Fryer manufacturing (deluge, formed, potato chip)", "Blancher manufacturing (belt, deluge, tri\u2011mode)", "Batter applicator systems", "Computational fluid dynamics (CFD) analysis", "Turnkey food processing line integration", "Global service network and remote diagnostics", "Maintenance and retrofit services", "Equipment sanitation and clean\u2011in\u2011place design"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Fried food production", "Potato processing", "Seafood processing", "Vegetable processing", "Snack food manufacturing", "Malting"], "materials": ["Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["Tri\u2011Mode Belt Blancher", "Deluge Fryer", "Formed Fryer", "Potato Chip Fryer", "Vibrating Conveyors", "Flodin Rock Trap", "Two Stage Tote Dumper", "Malting System", "Batter Applicators", "CO\u2011PRODUCT SERIES fryers", "Clean\u2011in\u2011Place Hood"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lowest total cost of ownership over a ten\u2011year horizon", "Exceptional service with urgent field response", "Continuous improvement through design and manufacturing enhancements", "CFD expertise optimizing oil flow and eliminating recirculation zones", "Global service network with remote diagnostics"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1968 in Woodburn, Oregon -> db", "Co\u2011founder Ed McKenney -> /about-us", "Acquired by FPS Food Process Solutions in 2023 -> /about-us", "Designs, builds, installs fryers and blanchers -> /", "Uses CFD modelling to optimize oil flow -> /", "Global service network & remote diagnostics -> /", "Operating philosophy: lowest total cost of ownership, exceptional service, continuous improvement -> /about-us", "Customers: General Foods, Ore\u2011Ida, Simplot, McCain, Lamb Weston -> /about-us", "Equipment lines: Tri\u2011Mode Belt Blancher, Deluge Fryer, Formed Fryer, Potato Chip Fryer, Vibrating Conveyors, Flodin Rock Trap, Two Stage Tote Dumper, Malting System, Batter Applicators, CO\u2011PRODUCT SERIES, Clean\u2011in\u2011Place Hood -> /about-us", "Stainless steel construction -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we design, build, and install the industry''s largest and most reliable fryers and blanchers", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gem-equipment-of-oregon-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
