UPDATE companies SET description='Gellco Clothing & Shoes was founded in 1959 in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. The company began as a single store serving the American worker with occupational footwear and work apparel.

Today the business operates five retail locations across Oklahoma City, Edmond, Broken Arrow, and Tulsa, supplemented by a fleet of six mobile shoe trucks that bring more than 1,000 pairs of safety footwear directly to job sites. The company stocks over 20 name brands and well over 200 styles of safety footwear, and is also one of Oklahoma''s largest providers of flame-resistant clothing and workwear. A central shipping center in Oklahoma allows delivery to most U.S. locations within three to five days. The organization employs approximately 5,000 people according to company records.

Gellco serves companies of all sizes, from small crews of five employees to workforces of 5,000, providing corporate safety footwear and flame-resistant clothing programs.

The company distinguishes itself through its mobile ShoeMobile service at no extra cost, a broad in-stock selection, and a focus on personal customer service that includes expert fitting, custom embroidery, flexible invoicing, and online ordering tools. Gellco''s staff are trained on OSHA PPE standards to ensure workers leave compliant for the job.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Corporate safety footwear programs", "Mobile on-site fitting service (ShoeMobile)", "Flame-resistant clothing programs", "Custom embroidery", "Online catalog and ordering", "Flexible invoicing and reporting", "Payroll deduction", "OSHA PPE compliance assistance", "Custom clothing packages", "Footwear accessories and clothing accessories"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "3-5 days for shipping to most US locations", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Six mobile shoe trucks that visit job sites at no extra charge", "Central Oklahoma shipping center reaching most U.S. locations in 3\u20135 days", "Over 20 safety footwear brands and 200+ styles in stock", "One of Oklahoma''s largest flame-resistant clothing providers", "Expert face-to-face fitting and OSHA PPE compliance assistance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1959 in Oklahoma City -> /about", "Five retail locations in Oklahoma City, Edmond, Broken Arrow, Tulsa -> /about", "Six mobile shoe trucks in fleet -> /about", "Over 20 name brands and 200+ styles in stock -> /about, /services", "Mobile trucks carry over 1,000 pairs -> /about", "Central shipping center reaches most US in 3-5 days -> /about", "One of Oklahoma''s largest FR clothing providers -> /about, /services", "Corporate programs for 5 to 5,000 employees -> /services", "Services include expert fitting, custom embroidery, flexible invoicing, reporting, online ordering, payroll deduction -> /services", "Staff trained on OSHA PPE standards -> /services", "Employee count 5000 -> db", "Headquarters Oklahoma City, Oklahoma -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Gellco Clothing & Shoes is Oklahoma''s leading provider of Safety Footwear. With over 20 name brands and well over 200 different styles in-stock we offer by far the largest selection in the great state of Oklahoma.", "founded_year": "1959", "employee_count": "5000", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gellco-work-outfitters' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Generac Power Systems was founded in 1959 in Waukesha, Wisconsin. The company began by engineering the first affordable home standby generators and developing an engine purpose-built for generator use.

Today Generac manufactures a broad portfolio of power products: portable, residential, commercial, and industrial generators; manual and fully automatic transfer switches for applications up to 2 MW; a mobile line of light towers, trailer-mounted generators, and combination units built for demanding environments; and a full range of residential, commercial, and industrial power washers. The company designs and builds its own engines and power equipment across multiple product lines.

Generac serves homeowners, contractors, and industrial facilities. Its residential standby generators are sold through authorized dealers to homeowners seeking backup power. Portable generators target campers, tailgaters, and workers needing mobile power. Commercial and industrial customers use its stationary generators and transfer switches for critical infrastructure. The mobile line serves a variety of industries requiring rugged, trailer-mounted power and lighting.

