UPDATE companies SET description='Geometric Innovations LLC was founded in 2009 by Jarrett Maxwell in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. Initially a general home remodeling business, the company shifted its focus to woodworking, specializing in fine furniture and custom cabinetry.

The shop produces custom furniture pieces and architectural millwork for both new construction and renovation projects. Its capabilities span custom furniture design and build, cabinetry for kitchens, bathrooms, and built-ins, as well as a variety of millwork services. Past projects include bedroom sets, credenzas, china cabinets, tables, lighting, mirror frames, entertainment centers, hidden bookcases, and vanities. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

Geometric Innovations serves private residential clients, interior designers, and architects across residential and commercial sectors. The company collaborates directly with design professionals to deliver pieces that integrate into larger architectural schemes.

Maxwell states that the company aims to blur the line between art and furniture while maintaining a firm grasp on form and function, with a stated goal of excellence in design, materials, construction, and client relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and build", "Cabinetry (new construction and remodel)", "Architectural millwork", "Woodworking"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Interior design", "Architecture"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom furniture design and build", "Cabinetry for new construction and remodel", "Architectural millwork capabilities", "Collaboration with designers and architects", "Focus on blending artistic design with functional craftsmanship"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 by Jarrett Maxwell in Oklahoma City, OK -> db", "Specializes in fine furniture and custom cabinetry -> /about", "Services: Custom Furniture Design & Build, Cabinetry, Millwork -> /about", "Serves private clients, designers, architects in residential and commercial settings -> /about", "Design philosophy: blur lines between art and furniture, excellence in design/materials/construction -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I founded Geometric Innovations in 2009 as a general home remodel company. After several years I began to specialize in woodworking with a focus on fine furniture and custom cabinetry.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='geometric-innovations-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='George T. Hall Company (GTH) was founded in 1932 in Anaheim, California, by George Hall. Now led by Chairman Chuck Niemann and President Dina Johnson, the company has operated for over nine decades under the motto "The House That Service Built," emphasizing continuous improvement and customer partnerships.

GTH is a full-service control solutions provider that designs, programs, and manufactures UL-certified custom control panels (UL508A/UL698A) in two panel shops located in California and Nevada. As a CSIA-certified system integrator since 2017, the firm combines control panel manufacturing, field services, system integration, and product distribution under one roof, supporting the full lifecycle from design and commissioning to preventative maintenance and optimization.

The company serves public and private industrial organizations across the western United States, with documented expertise in water and wastewater, mining/minerals/metals, food and beverage, pharmaceutical and life sciences, general manufacturing, and aerospace. Its MSHA- and BROWZ-certified engineers deliver rugged controls for hazardous environments, while ISA- and FDA-aligned capabilities address regulated sectors.

