UPDATE companies SET description='Gilbert Creek Woodworks operates from Menomonie, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1987 by Duane Zweber. After three decades as a production manager and head of product design for two large woodworking firms, Zweber launched his own shop to serve clients seeking custom wood products. Today the business remains a family affair, with his sons Brian and Robert contributing finishing expertise and business management respectively.

The company produces a range of custom woodwork, including kitchen cabinets, office furniture, entertainment centers, architectural millwork, and other specialty pieces. Projects are built for residential, commercial, and one-off commissions, though the facility size and annual volume are not disclosed.

The shop handles everything from single-room cabinetry to full-office fit-outs and custom entertainment centers, but no specific client names or industry certifications are published.

