UPDATE companies SET description='Global Bridge Pharmaceutical operates from Charlotte, North Carolina, as a pharmacist-led pharmaceutical distribution and consulting company. It was established by professionals with a combined 55 years of experience across healthcare, drug regulation, and supply chain management, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The company provides Rx procurement, pharmacovigilance and drug safety services, global and managed access programs, and export and donor initiatives. Its core services include strategic pharmaceutical sourcing, hospital supply chain support, drug shortage and emergency procurement, managed access and patient support programs, repurposing of excess pharmaceuticals, and global access and export solutions. The team leverages an agile network of licensed suppliers, wholesalers, specialty pharmacies, and industry partners to deliver compliant, cost-effective solutions.

Global Bridge serves hospitals and health systems, clinics and pharmacies, government agencies and non-governmental organizations, and pharmaceutical manufacturers seeking distribution and access partners. It also supports public health programs and charitable clinics, particularly in North Carolina and other states where it holds licenses.

The company differentiates itself through its pharmacist-led expertise, regulatory awareness (USFDA-registered and DSCSA-compliant), and social impact initiatives such as RxSecondHome™, which redirects excess and short-dated medicines to underserved populations. Its mission emphasizes collaboration with healthcare professionals to improve access to safe, affordable, and high-quality medicines worldwide.', certifications=ARRAY['USFDA registered','DSCSA compliant','Minority Business Entity (MBE) certified','SAM registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rx Procurement", "Pharmacovigilance & Drug Safety Services", "Managed Access & Patient Support Programs", "Global Access & Export Solutions", "Strategic Pharmaceutical Sourcing", "Hospital Supply Chain Support", "Drug Shortage & Emergency Procurement", "Repurposing excess pharmaceutical", "Drug information and consulting services", "Export & Donor Programs"], "industries": ["Hospitals & Health Systems", "Clinics & Pharmacies", "Governments & NGOs", "Manufacturers", "Public health organizations"], "materials": ["Prescription medicines", "Pharmaceutical products", "Excess and short-dated pharmaceutical inventory"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pharmacist-led team with combined 55 years of healthcare and regulatory experience", "SAM registered and USFDA registered", "Agile network of licensed suppliers and industry partners", "Social impact program RxSecondHome\u2122 redirecting excess medicines"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina -> /", "Pharmacist-led pharmaceutical distribution and consulting company -> /", "Certified Minority Business Entity (MBE) and HUBZone certified -> /about-us", "SAM registered and USFDA registered -> /about-us", "CAGE code 8F8E7 -> /about-us", "Combined 55 years of experience -> /about-us", "Services: Rx Procurement, Pharmacovigilance, Managed Access, Export & Donor Programs -> /services", "Industries served: Hospitals & Health Systems, Clinics & Pharmacies, Governments & NGOs, Manufacturers -> /", "Social impact initiative RxSecondHome\u2122 -> /about-us", "Offices in US, Italy, Cameroon -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Global Bridge Pharmaceutical is a pharmacist-led pharmaceutical distribution and consulting company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "8F8E7", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["U.S. FDA export compliance"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Minority-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='global-bridge-pharmaceutical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Global Electronics is based in New Baltimore, Michigan.

The firm develops and supplies automotive emissions calibration and end‑of‑line testing equipment. Its product line includes the Misfire Generator, Dual‑Channel O₂ Fault Simulator, USD II automatic transmission solenoid test system, a radio‑frequency identification (RFID) signal tracking system, and an engine powertrain simulator. In addition to hardware, Global Electronics provides manufacturing and engineering services such as PLC re‑engineering, prototyping, assembly, wire‑harness fabrication, circuit‑board production, and design‑support teams that can be configured for specific applications.

Customers are primarily automotive original‑equipment manufacturers and their tier‑one suppliers, along with broader transportation‑industry clients. The company also pursues work transitioning government‑developed technologies — such as situational‑awareness systems, artificial‑intelligence tools, geo‑fencing, virtual‑reality interfaces, and commercial‑vehicle powertrain electronics — into civilian markets.

Global Electronics says its differentiator is a project‑selection strategy that favors contracts which yield generic products reusable in other markets, allowing development costs to be amortized across multiple customers. It also emphasizes its experience with PLC migrations and its ability to assemble experienced engineering teams for varied delivery models.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic design and development", "Emissions calibration", "End-of-line testing", "Misfire generation", "O\u2082 fault simulation", "Automatic transmission solenoid testing", "RFID signal tracking", "Powertrain simulation", "PLC re-engineering", "Prototyping", "Assembly", "Manufacturing", "Wire harness fabrication", "Circuit board production", "Analog signal modification", "Cam timing fault simulation", "Breakout box fabrication", "Support services", "Supplier project tracking applications"], "industries": ["Automotive OEMs", "Automotive suppliers", "Transportation industry", "Government/defense", "Commercial vehicle"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Project strategy that creates generic products reusable across multiple markets", "Experience with PLC migration and re\u2011engineering", "Configurable engineering teams for design and support services", "Development of government\u2011to\u2011civilian technologies (AI, VR, geo\u2011fencing, commercial\u2011vehicle powertrain)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: New Baltimore, MI -> /", "Products: Misfire Generator, Dual Channel O2 Fault Simulator, USD II, RFID Signal Tracking System, Powertrain Simulator -> /", "Services: PLC Re-Engineering, Support Services, manufacturing and engineering services -> /services", "Industries: Automotive OEMs and suppliers, transportation industry, government/defense, commercial vehicle -> /", "Differentiator: focus on generic products for other markets -> /", "Differentiator: uniquely positioned for PLC migration -> /services", "Advanced development: government to civilian applications (AI, VR, geo-fencing, commercial vehicle powertrain) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Global Electronics develops and supplies automotive emissions calibration and end of line testing products to Automotive OEM\u2019s and suppliers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='global-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Global Steering Systems is headquartered in Watertown, Connecticut. The company was founded more than four decades ago as an independent, privately held business and remains under private ownership.

The company reports a decades-long track record of excellence and production capabilities across North America, Asia Pacific, and Europe. It designs and manufactures steering components including column shafts, U-joints, center-mounted support bearings, and complex intermediate shafts for column-drive and rack-drive applications. A proprietary high-performance spline slider is produced in-house. Operations are supported by a full-service test lab that validates products at every manufacturing step and a full-service engineering group that handles design, analysis, risk assessment, prototyping, and validation testing. GSS operates facilities in Connecticut (headquarters, R&D, and manufacturing), Michigan (sales and support), Changshu, China (manufacturing, sales, and support), Opole, Poland (manufacturing, R&D, sales, and support), and Ponta Grossa, Brazil (sales and support).

GSS serves the automotive industry, supplying light- and heavy-duty vehicle platforms. Its customer base includes major OEMs such as Ford Motor Company, Jeep, Lucid Motors, and General Motors.

