UPDATE companies SET description='GlobalFoundries is headquartered in Malta, New York, and was founded in 2009 as a joint venture between Mubadala Investment Company and Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) to address growing global demand for advanced semiconductors. The company''s first major U.S. fabrication facility began construction in Malta in 2013, becoming a cornerstone of its advanced manufacturing strategy.

Its technology portfolio spans CMOS, FinFET, FDX™ FD-SOI, BCD, Power GaN, RF-SOI, SiGe, RF GaN, silicon photonics, and quantum-process platforms. Manufacturing sites include Malta (global headquarters), Burlington, Vermont (RF and GaN center of excellence), Dresden, Germany, Singapore, and Guangzhou, China, with a workforce of 5,000–9,999 employees.

GlobalFoundries serves aerospace and defense, automotive, data-center and communications infrastructure, home and industrial IoT, and smart mobile device markets. Customers include companies such as Marvell, which collaborates on high-performance SiGe technology for optical connectivity, and the firm has partnered with TSMC to establish a U.S.-based supply of silicon interposers for advanced CoWoS® packaging. The MIPS subsidiary provides processor IP and virtual platforms for software-to-silicon development.

The company emphasizes differentiation through deep co-innovation with customers, governments, and universities, combining R&D, IP, design, and manufacturing across a flexible global footprint. Its stated mission is to deliver trusted, essential chips that enable AI at scale from the cloud to the physical world, with a quality philosophy targeting zero excursions and zero defects.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor foundry services", "Wafer fabrication (200mm and 300mm)", "Advanced packaging (2.5D/3D, wafer-to-wafer, die-to-wafer bonding, interposer-based)", "CMOS process technology", "FDX FD-SOI", "FinFET", "BCD (Bipolar-CMOS-DMOS)", "Power GaN", "RF-SOI", "SiGe (Silicon Germanium)", "RF GaN", "Silicon photonics", "Quantum technology process platforms", "Wafer bumping (SnAg, copper pillar, WLCSP)", "Wafer sort with Known Good Die methodology", "Backside grind, wafer bake, dicing, marking, binning", "Module packaging and assembly", "RF testing (high/low temperature, analog/digital TxRx, memory, high-speed interface, high-voltage/current)", "ATE test program development", "Engineering services (design for manufacturing, package engineering, reliability stress, debugging)", "Reliability qualification (JEDEC, MIL-STD, AEC)", "Custom silicon design and IP integration", "Processor IP (MIPS) and virtual platforms", "Turnkey manufacturing from design to final test"], "industries": ["Aerospace & defense", "Automotive", "Data center & communications infrastructure", "Home & industrial IoT", "Smart mobile devices", "Microelectronics", "Wireless", "IoT"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Silicon Germanium (SiGe)", "Gallium Nitride (GaN)", "Silicon-on-Insulator (SOI)", "Silicon interposers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 as joint venture between Mubadala and AMD -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Malta, New York -> /about-us, db", "Employee count 5000-9999 -> db", "O