UPDATE companies SET description='Grace Technologies is headquartered in Davenport, Iowa. The company traces its roots to 1993 when founder Phil Allen, then a startup system integrator called Grace Engineering, encountered a hazardous electrical safety issue during a friction welder retrofit at John Deere. The solution he devised—a panel interface connector branded GracePort—launched the business, which later became Grace Engineered Products and, in 2020, Grace Technologies.

Today Grace manufactures three core product lines: GracePort panel interface connectors that provide thru-door access to PLCs and control panels; GracePESDs, permanent electrical safety devices that combine presence-of-voltage LED indication with absence-of-voltage test points for lockout/tagout; and the GraceSense predictive maintenance system, a line of IIoT smart sensors that continuously monitor vibration and temperature on switchgear, transformers, and rotating equipment. The catalog encompasses roughly 16,000 SKUs, and the company ships orders worldwide within two to three business days through a distribution network spanning more than 60 countries.

Customers include power plants, food and beverage facilities, chiller plants, and any operation that relies on evaporative cooling towers, as well as broader industrial facilities seeking to reduce incident energy exposure and unplanned downtime. The company’s predictive maintenance webinar series, co-hosted with Infinite Cooling, targets managers of those specific asset types.

Grace says its differentiation rests on four pillars: thought leadership from a team of forward‑thinking engineers; mass customization enabled by its deep SKU count; fast delivery via the 2‑3‑day global shipping promise; and a founding principle of being easy to do business with. Its stated mission is to pursue practical ways of keeping live voltage away from workers before, during, and after maintenance tasks, while empowering maintenance programs with IIoT sensor data.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Panel interface connectors", "Permanent Electrical Safety Devices (PESDs)", "Absence of voltage indicators", "Presence of voltage indicators", "Lockout/Tagout (LOTO) solutions", "Predictive maintenance monitoring", "IIoT smart sensor deployment", "Vibration monitoring", "Temperature monitoring", "Remote asset health monitoring", "Customizable access programming ports", "Thru-door connectivity for PLCs"], "industries": ["Power generation", "Food and beverage", "Chiller plants", "Evaporative cooling tower operations", "Industrial facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Mass customization with approximately 16,000 SKUs", "Global shipping within 2\u20133 business days", "Founding principle: easy to do business with", "IIoT predictive maintenance sensors for continuous vibration and temperature monitoring"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1993 -> /about-us", "Founder Phil Allen -> /about-us", "Headquarters Davenport, Iowa -> db", "Products: GracePort, GracePESDs, GraceSense -> /about-us", "16,000 SKUs -> /about-us", "Ships worldwide in 2-3 business days -> /about-us", "Global distribution in 60+ countries -> /about-us", "Industries: power plants, food and beverage, chiller plants, cooling towers -> /", "Mission: keep live voltage away from workers -> /about-us", "Mass customization, fast delivery, easy to do business -> /about-us", "Thought leadership team -> /about-us", "IIoT sensors for vibration and temperature monitoring -> /about-us", "GracePort panel interface connectors -> /about-us", "GracePESDs for LOTO -> /about-us", "GraceSense predictive maintenance system -> /about-us", "Name change to Grace Technologies in 2020 -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Grace manufacturers and delivers electrical safety innovations and predictive maintenance solutions through a global distribution network", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='grace-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Grado Creations is based in Albuquerque, New Mexico, and traces its origins to 1998 when master craftsman Jose Grado began building custom furniture and cabinetry with a Southwest aesthetic. The workshop initially focused on hand-carved wood pieces, bespoke kitchen cabinets, and one-of-a-kind furniture for homes and retailers across the United States.

Today the company has pivoted entirely to premium made-to-order home textiles. Its product line includes all-season quilted bedding sets, reversible water-resistant sofa slipcovers, absorbent area rugs and floor mats, and seasonal accents such as quilted tree skirts and laundry organizers. Production uses advanced direct-to-textile dye technology on high-density microfiber and poly-cotton blends, with multi-layer quilting, hypoallergenic batting, and reinforced perimeter stitching. Every item is printed, cut, and sewn individually after an order is placed, avoiding warehouse overstock.

The brand serves the home decor and lifestyle market, targeting consumers who want rustic, Southwestern-inspired textiles that withstand daily use by pets and children. Its direct-to-consumer channel ships nationwide, and the product assortment — exemplified by pet-proof sofa covers, machine-washable quilts, and cabin-themed bedding — is designed for practical, lived-in spaces.

Grado Creations says its differentiation lies in four pillars: authentic heritage-inspired designs rooted in Southwestern and lodge aesthetics; engineering for real-life durability (water-resistant, non-slip, machine-washable); a conscious made-to-order model that reduces textile waste; and transparent, US-based customer support with free shipping on orders over $150 and a 30-day return window.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Made-to-order home textile manufacturing", "Direct-to-textile dye printing", "Multi-layer quilting with water-resistant barriers", "Precision stitching and reinforced perimeter seams", "Hypoallergenic batting insertion", "Custom sizing and design for bedding, slipcovers, rugs, accents"], "industries": ["Home decor", "Home textiles", "Bedding", "Furniture protection", "Pet-friendly home products", "Rustic/Southwestern style home goods"], "materials": ["High-density microfiber", "Poly-cotton fabric blends", "Hypoallergenic batting", "Water-resistant barrier fabric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "3-5 business days handling, 5-8 business days transit (8-13 business days total)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Heritage-inspired Southwestern and rustic lodge designs", "Engineered for real life: water-resistant, pet-friendly, machine-washable", "Mindful made-to-order production \u2014 no mass inventory", "Direct-to-textile dye printing for vibrant, fade-resistant patterns", "Free US shipping on orders over $150; 30-day hassle-free returns"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Founded 1998, led by Jose Grado -> db (description)", "Transition from woodwork to home textiles -> /about-us", "Product categories: quilted bedding, sofa slipcovers, area rugs, home accents -> /about-us", "Made-to-order production with direct-to-textile dye printing -> / (FAQ) and /about-us", "Materials: high-density microfiber, poly-cotton, hypoallergenic batting, water-resistant barriers -> /about-us", 